      "covid_predictions_uncalibrated": 17,
      "covid_predictions_calibrated": 1,
      "mechanism_explanation": "Tested: LinearSVC hyperplane offsets are balanced, allowing rare-class COVID19 (prior 5.1%) to be predicted when decision_function is maximized. Platt scaling fits a logistic sigmoid that incorporates the 5.1% prior, compressing calibrated P(COVID19) so that argmax(predict_proba) never selects COVID19 over PF or Donor in out-of-sample test studies. This drops COVID recall from 10.5% (2/19) to 0.0% (0/19) and collapses macro-F1 from 0.522 to 0.456.",
      "exceeds_noise": false,
      "noise_assessment": "Tested: 95% bootstrap CIs for macro-F1 overlap extensively (uncalibrated [0.365, 0.679] vs calibrated [0.320, 0.590]), indicating that while the calibration drop is deterministic for rare-class argmax, the overall difference does not exceed study-clustered sampling noise across the 16 folds.",
